{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00428","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00428@rel:R25-11#d8a62427","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00428","release":"R25-11","content":"function SetFileSize [SWS_PER_00428] Upstream: RS_PER_00001 , RS_PER_00004 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_ AP_00128, RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; SetFileSize ( std::uint64_t size) noexcept; Reduces the size of the file to ’size’, effectively removing the current content of the file beyond this size. The current file position is unchanged if it is lower than ’size’, or set to the last valid position in the file otherwise. If ’size’ is 0, the current file position will also be set to 0. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/write_accessor.h\" class mono Scope class ara::per::WriteAccessor class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit not thread-safe PerErrc ::kPhysical no_rollback_semantics class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td size td New size of the file. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; void &gt; td A Result of void. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td StorageFailure td Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kValidationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the validity of stored data cannot be ensured. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the encryption or decryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kInvalidSize td rollback_semantics Returned if the new size is larger than the current size. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if calculating or checking the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00428